AFS-001 — Foundation Principles

Document ID: AFS-001
Title: Foundation Principles
Version: 1.0.0-draft
Status: Draft

1. Purpose

This specification establishes the foundational technical principles of the Atlas Engineering Cognition Framework (AECF).

The Atlas Foundation Specification (AFS) defines the common technical infrastructure, architectural principles, and shared conventions that apply uniformly across every Atlas specification family.

AFS provides the normative foundation upon which all Atlas specifications are constructed, ensuring consistency, interoperability, extensibility, and long-term architectural stability.

2. Scope

This specification defines:

Foundation architecture
Technical principles
Shared infrastructure
Cross-specification consistency
Common conventions
Inheritance rules
Foundation governance
Evolution principles

This specification applies to every Atlas specification family, profile, implementation, and extension.

3. Canonical Definition

The Atlas Foundation Specification (AFS) is the normative technical foundation that defines the common infrastructure, conventions, and architectural principles shared by every Atlas specification.

AFS provides shared infrastructure.

It SHALL NOT define domain-specific engineering behavior.

4. Objectives

The Atlas Foundation Specification SHALL:

Establish a common technical foundation.
Eliminate duplication across specifications.
Standardize shared infrastructure.
Enable interoperability.
Preserve consistency.
Support extensibility.
Enable long-term evolution.
Maintain implementation independence.
