APS Policies
AWS Workflows
AIS Cognitive Objects

Inheritance SHALL preserve canonical semantics.

9. Foundation Governance

The Atlas Foundation SHALL be governed through:

Constitutional Authority (ACC)
Foundation Review Board
Technical Steering Committee
Specification Editors
Independent Reviewers

Governance SHALL ensure long-term architectural consistency.

10. Foundation Evolution

The Atlas Foundation SHALL evolve according to the following principles:

Shared concepts SHALL evolve before dependent specifications.
Dependent specifications SHALL reference foundation revisions explicitly.
Foundation evolution SHALL preserve implementation stability.
Major revisions SHALL include migration guidance.
11. Foundation Quality

Every Foundation Specification SHALL satisfy:

Correctness
Consistency
Simplicity
Reusability
Extensibility
Interoperability
Explainability
Long-term maintainability

Quality SHALL be independently verifiable.

12. Conformance

A specification conforms to AFS if it:

References applicable Foundation Specifications.
Does not redefine shared concepts.
Preserves Foundation semantics.
Maintains interoperability.
Supports extension mechanisms.
Preserves implementation independence.
13. Future Evolution

Future revisions MAY introduce:

Additional shared infrastructure services.
New serialization formats.
Enhanced interoperability mechanisms.
Distributed identity frameworks.
AI-native foundation services.
Formal semantic verification.

Extensions SHALL preserve foundational architectural principles.

